# A destruct takes no arguments: drop x calls x.destruct(), so what it needs (a manager) is kept in a field.

### Holds a block from a manager.
entity Holder
    data: Addr

### A holder of nothing.
### :returns: The holder.
common routine Holder.construct() -> Me
    return Me(data: .hollow())

### Gives the block back to `manager`.
### :param manager: Where the block came from.
routine @Holder.destruct(manager: @MemoryManager) -> None
    return

routine start() -> None
    return
